  "text": "The farmer now has 27 sheep in total. To determine the correct amount, we first examine the classic riddle phrasing that states all but 9 sheep run away. Rather than subtracting nine from seventeen, this phrasing explicitly tells us that exactly 9 sheep remained on the property while the others ran off. Following that event, the farmer decides to purchase twice as many sheep as currently remain. Because there are 9 sheep remaining, twice that specific amount comes out to 18 newly bought animals. To calculate the final total, we simply add the 9 original sheep that stayed to the 18 sheep that were newly purchased, giving a grand total of exactly 27 sheep currently living on the farmer's land.\n",
